  "method": "Native saved-board polygons, with outline holes preserved. F.Cu and B.Cu geometry is unioned per physical UUID and projected onto the same XY plane. A spatial-index lower-bound search covers every opposite-domain pair below 1.5mm; query-nearest separately finds the global minimum. Native polygon comparison permits only the declared 0.0011mm numerical epsilon; near-boundary pairs and the strict uncertainty lower bound are also reported.",
  "limitations": [
    "Saved zone fill is measured exactly as loaded. This tool never refills or saves CAD and cannot prove that a cached fill was regenerated after the last route/outline edit; the final caller must run native full refill/save and freeze its SHA before this audit.",
    "Pad/via outer envelopes are conservative: drill interiors are not used as safe passage for opposite-domain copper. Paste-only and other non-copper-layer shapes have no F.Cu/B.Cu geometry.",
    "XY projection deliberately rejects cross-face overlap; it does not calculate a 3D insulation path through FR4, air clearance, enclosure creepage, slots, voltage ratings or isolation component certification.",
    "A passing result applies only to the bound source files and stated numerical tolerance. Native connectivity/parity DRC, same-face production clearances, solder assembly and EMC remain separate requirements."
  ]
